This is only true in a country in North America, namely USA. Other
countries like Canada and European countries have ratified a convention
which does not demand these formal requirements to copyright-protect
works. There (C) 1986 Joe Random is OK. And material published in USA
and at the same time published in these other countries retain their
copyrights in the other countries, although they do not get protection
in USA.


